                <pb facs="hu_d24-1" n="1" xml:id="ni_d24-1"/>

                <head>NI–24. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On November 11, 1960, a group of Nicaraguan insurgents, estimated between 150 and
                    300, staged a number of armed attacks against administrative and National Guard
                    facilities in the towns of Jinotepe and Diriamba. Within the next twenty-four
                    hours, the Nicaraguan National Guard retook the two cities and were engaged in
                    subduing the insurgents. By November 15, about fifty rebels, pursued by the
                    National Guard crossed the border into Costa Rica. Documentation on the uprising
                    is in file 717.00.</p>
            </div>
